  "worked_solution": "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{\u2218}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({270}^{\u2218})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${270}^{\u2218}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${270}^{\u2218}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n$$\n{270}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218}=-{90}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-1)=-{90}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
